      "sourceTextSha256": "1eea98d9ca7c4ef5654a833abcfe8f4e1983a8cb27fed76986e622547b7826ea",
      "text": "Antarctica is one of the most remote and inaccessible places on Earth: the coldest, highest, windiest, driest and least inhabited continent on the planet. An enigmatic and extraordinary territory, where much of our planet’s history remains preserved beneath enormous layers of ice. A pristine place devoted to peace, exploration and science.\n\nOn board our aircraft, you will fly over the Strait of Magellan, Tierra del Fuego and the Darwin Cordillera, before reaching the legendary Cape Horn and crossing the notorious Drake Passage.\n\nFinally, you will land on King George Island, the gateway to the Antarctic continent. This is where your experience on Antarctic territory will begin.",
